WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:01.790
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:09.150
As far as eccentric billionaires go Alabama-based
George W. Barber is high on the list.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:16.119
He owns the world's largest motorcycle collection
and his own private race track but when you've

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:19.939
ticked those off your list what else do you
do with your endless money?

00:00:19.939 --> 00:00:26.089
Well, in the 90s Barber used his wealth to
have a handful of life-sized dinosaurs built

00:00:26.089 --> 00:00:32.480
and placed randomly around the 10,000 acre
woodlands surrounding his home.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:38.610
The dinosaurs are also accompanied by a collection
of medieval knight statues.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:42.320
But he didn't stop there.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:49.750
Barber also commissioned a life-sized fibreglass
replica of stone henge that he hilariously

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:51.170
named Bamahenge.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:58.000
And to top it all off a 50 foot naked woman
submerged in his private Marina.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.790
So despite the fact that if you become a billionaire
you'll have vastly more money than you know

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:07.440
what to do with, and you'll have to resort
to building giant dinosaurs and women, the

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.500
desire to be one is great.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.120
Let's not lie to ourselves, most people would
love to be a billionaire, even if we don't

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:18.790
know why or how we would spend our fortune.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:25.450
But the unlucky reality is that your chances
of amassing one billion dollars or pounds

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:31.220
worth of assets within your lifetime are pitifully
slim.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:40.430
The current population is 7.5 billion and
there are 2,043 billionaires in the world

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:50.560
today, meaning the chance of you becoming
a billionaire is 0.000027%.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.750
So should you just give up now?

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:58.200
No, because you can of course increase your
chances.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:05.850
You see billionaires aren't like you and I.
Their behaviours and actions are very different

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.590
and unusual.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:15.689
And statistics show that copying these behaviours
won't guarantee that you'll become a billionaire

00:02:15.689 --> 00:02:20.159
but it vastly increases your chances.

00:02:20.159 --> 00:02:26.010
Firstly they are patient, far more patient
than the average person.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:31.129
Billionaire investor Warren Buffet once said
"The stock market is a device for transferring

00:02:31.129 --> 00:02:35.400
money from the impatient to the patient."

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.840
Most people want success overnight and it's
easy to feel like you've failed if you don't

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:44.480
achieve it and one's natural instinct is to
beat yourself up over failure or just slow

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.709
growth.

00:02:45.709 --> 00:02:49.379
But patience is the key to success.

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:54.409
The world's wealthiest individuals are no
strangers to failure and having to wait, sometimes

00:02:54.409 --> 00:02:58.269
decades, for success to come along due to
their hard efforts.

00:02:58.269 --> 00:03:06.249
Bill Gates, the richest person on the planet
knows this all too well.

00:03:06.249 --> 00:03:09.529
You've heard of Microsoft, but have you heard
of Traff-O-Data?

00:03:09.529 --> 00:03:12.879
No, that's because it was a huge flop.

00:03:12.879 --> 00:03:15.879
Traff-O-Data was Mr Gate's first company.

00:03:15.879 --> 00:03:20.329
Its goal was "to read the raw data from roadway
traffic counters and create reports for traffic

00:03:20.329 --> 00:03:21.329
engineers".

00:03:21.329 --> 00:03:27.430
Gates thought his genius idea would optimise
traffic and end road congestion forever.

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:33.269
But the technology didn't work and it fell
flat on its face.

00:03:33.269 --> 00:03:40.579
But Gates had patience and perseverance, and
from the ashes of Traff-O-Data, Microsoft

00:03:40.579 --> 00:03:42.049
was born.

00:03:42.049 --> 00:03:49.750
Since then Microsoft has created 3 billionaires
and over 12,000 millionaires.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:04:00.249
James Dyson created an incredible 5,127 vacuum
prototypes over 15 years before he finally

00:04:00.249 --> 00:04:03.999
took his first bagless vacuum to market.

00:04:03.999 --> 00:04:07.480
Thomas Edison famously said "I have not failed.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:11.489
I’ve just found 10,000 ways that won’t
work."

00:04:11.489 --> 00:04:17.789
From Steve Jobs to Richard Branson, they all
had to fail miserably before they found success.

00:04:17.789 --> 00:04:23.970
If they had been impatient they may have thrown
in the towel and achieved nothing.

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:27.100
Billionaires are the world's best problem
solvers.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.650
Solving problems is how most made their fortunes.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:36.289
But the road to riches is often fraught with
seemingly impossible obstacles.

00:04:36.289 --> 00:04:41.879
When Joseph Piscopo was starting up his software
company Pansophic it was going fantastically

00:04:41.879 --> 00:04:47.950
well for a few years, with $230 million of
annual revenue.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:55.280
Until one New Year's Eve in 1985, a disgruntled
employee walked through the company's data

00:04:55.280 --> 00:05:04.020
centre with an industrial strength electro-magnet,
erasing every single hard drive in the building.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:09.300
This was a complete disaster, they had no
external backups and everyone thought the

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.139
company would close its doors for good.

00:05:11.139 --> 00:05:19.080
But a defiant Piscopo set to work on rebuilding
all the lost data, within two weeks the data

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:23.479
was restored and the company was flourishing
again.

00:05:23.479 --> 00:05:30.300
Rock Mackie, founder of a billion-dollar cancer-treatment
company called TomoTherapy, encountered an

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.039
entrepreneurs worst nightmare.

00:05:33.039 --> 00:05:39.349
Right at the launch of his company, the main
investor pulled out on launch day and Mackie

00:05:39.349 --> 00:05:43.260
had to fire all of his employees on the spot.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:50.099
Yet despite the incredible odds against him,
Mackie still managed to go public with TomoTherapy

00:05:50.099 --> 00:05:52.470
for a billion dollar valuation.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:58.310
There are also small, everyday behaviours
that most billionaires share.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:00.800
They are all very early risers, for example.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:08.531
Apple CEO Tim Cook, General Motors CEO Dan
Akerson and Disney CEO Robert Iger have all

00:06:08.531 --> 00:06:12.670
reported that they wake up at 4:30 every morning.

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:20.240
And according to research the vast majority
of billionaires are awake by at least 5:30am.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:24.889
Our brains are at their best in the morning,
and without the distractions of other people

00:06:24.889 --> 00:06:31.099
and family obligations, it's amazing what
one can accomplish in just one day.

00:06:31.099 --> 00:06:36.310
New York based Billionaire Irwin Simon wakes
up at 5 am and he says that he accomplishes

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:41.919
more before 9 am than most people do all day.

00:06:41.919 --> 00:06:46.630
He spends the early hours of the morning answering
emails, calling and managing his operations

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.360
in Europe and Asia.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:54.470
He prays, walks the dog and exercises, all
before his kids wake up.

00:06:54.470 --> 00:07:00.080
Oh and he even has time to sit down for breakfast
in Manhattan before arriving at his office

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:02.689
to start his actual work day.

00:07:02.689 --> 00:07:08.789
But surely if all these billionaires are waking
up so early they must be going to bed ridiculously

00:07:08.789 --> 00:07:10.240
early too?

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:16.050
No, quite the opposite, these individuals
have the rare ability to function at maximum

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:19.139
capacity on very little sleep.

00:07:19.139 --> 00:07:24.999
A study identified a small group of people,
roughly 2% of the population, who can function

00:07:24.999 --> 00:07:31.629
and live very happily on very little sleep,
just a few hours each night.

00:07:31.629 --> 00:07:37.349
This isn't just willpower though, researchers
actually found that these people carry a mutation

00:07:37.349 --> 00:07:40.499
of a gene called hDEC2.

00:07:40.499 --> 00:07:45.419
When they tweaked the same gene and put it
into mice, they found that the mice began

00:07:45.419 --> 00:07:49.169
to sleep less, just like the human test subjects.

00:07:49.169 --> 00:07:56.749
It's therefore a biological gift for a lucky
2%, that have been named the "Sleepless Elite".

00:07:56.749 --> 00:08:03.599
And what's even more amazing is that these
same people tend to be highly successful,

00:08:03.599 --> 00:08:08.469
many millionaires, billionaires, prime ministers
and presidents have been found to possess

00:08:08.469 --> 00:08:11.689
this gift of not needing much sleep.

00:08:11.689 --> 00:08:16.379
Thomas Jefferson, Benjamin Franklin and Leonardo
da Vinci are just a few people who were known

00:08:16.379 --> 00:08:18.550
to have this unusual gift.

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:24.949
Although there are some successful people
who didn't have this gift, yet they actually

00:08:24.949 --> 00:08:31.050
forced themselves to sleep less so they could
get more done, Margaret Thatcher trained herself

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:34.960
to only sleep for four hours every single
night.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:38.770
I can easier sympathise with Winston Churchill
though.

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:43.840
He begrudged getting out of bed so much that
he would spend the entire morning working

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:48.270
from his bed and even received important visitors
in his bedroom.

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:55.980
But if we put these smaller attributes of
billionaires aside, there's one major, glaring

00:08:55.980 --> 00:09:01.510
trait you absolutely must have to become very,
very wealthy.

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:09.650
To control such a large portion of the world's
wealth, you have to be a total psychopath

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:12.200
or at the very least a sociopath.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:18.500
And I'm not being sycophantic, most billionaires
are clinical psychopaths.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:23.540
Sam Wilkin is an economist and head of business
research at Oxford Economics.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:28.550
He has long studied and also wrote a book
about the world's wealthiest 1% and the common

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:30.320
factors that they share.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:37.051
And in all his time studying hundreds of wealthy
tycoons he discovered one common factor, they

00:09:37.051 --> 00:09:43.150
are willing to do absolutely anything to gain
market monopoly and ruthlessly force their

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:45.880
competitors into the ground.

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:52.080
I'm not saying that all billionaires are serial
killers but like serial killers, most are

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:54.600
unable to feel empathy.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:59.560
This helps them to make difficult decisions
that may harm others but will advance their

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:01.070
own goals.

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:07.070
Criminal psychologist Robert Hare famously
discovered, through his research that 1% of

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:14.150
the general population are categorised as
psychopaths, however, over 10% of financial

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:19.650
traders, stock brokers and bankers are psychopaths.

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:24.840
Being a psychopath doesn't mean you're going
to massacre your own family with a chainsaw.

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:31.150
Psychopathy is simply a condition that is
easily diagnosed by having the following traits,

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:37.510
superficially charming, highly manipulative
and able to con others, a complete lack of

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:42.830
empathy or remorse and a willingness to take
large risks.

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:48.220
So I basically just described Donald Trump
and probably any other billionaire you can

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:49.580
think of.

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:56.230
But perhaps there's a reason billionaires
are psychopaths, because it's what's required

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:58.170
to make it to the top.

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:04.860
In a crazily competitive capitalist society,
only those who are willing to take large risks,

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:10.180
and skirt around the edges of the law, perhaps
even break them from time to time are going

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:17.280
to gain that competitive edge needed to obliterate
the competition and monopolise a market.

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:23.070
Think Facebook, YouTube, Google, Amazon, they
are so wildly successful and are able to grow

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:30.570
with astonishing velocity, because they have
no effective competitors and that's the way

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:32.190
they like it.

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:37.740
It has long been rumoured that Bill Gates
stole the idea of Windows from his Apple colleagues.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:46.740
Warren Buffett pays income tax on only 0.018%
of his 74.2 billion dollars worth of assets,

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:51.660
whilst the rest of us are paying between 25
and 60 percent tax.

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:55.450
And then there are the billionaires that made
their wealth from poisoning the waters with

00:11:55.450 --> 00:12:01.430
nuclear waste, all the South American drug
barons, those who got wealthy on blood diamonds

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:07.010
and of course the billionaires who made their
wealth building and selling arms, used to

00:12:07.010 --> 00:12:10.920
slaughter millions of innocent people.

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:18.290
To do these things without remorse one has
to have a degree of psychopathy about them.

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:22.170
This doesn't mean that all billionaires are
bad people, quite the opposite.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:30.060
But there is undeniably a certain meglomanic
quality and a specific set of attributes required

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:32.790
to amass vast sums of wealth.

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:38.090
But of course the best way to increase your
chances of becoming a billionaire is not by

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:43.480
studying and copying other billionaire's behaviours
but by getting out there and putting your

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:47.450
every fibre into whatever you're passionate
about.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:52.970
Because success comes to those who are too
busy to be looking for it.

00:12:52.970 --> 00:13:10.920
Thanks for watching.

